  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Choose the correct statement(s):<br />A. Beryllium oxide is purely acidic in nature.<br />B. Beryllium carbonate is kept in the atmosphere of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.<br />C. Beryllium sulphate is readily soluble in water.<br />D. Beryllium shows anomalous behavior.<br />Choose the correct answer from the options given below:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eH7wu",
      "text": "A, B and C only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "spOqV",
      "text": "&nbsp;B,C and&nbsp;D only",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FSfqd",
      "text": "A&nbsp; and B only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JmMDx",
      "text": "A only",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A. Beryllium oxide is amphoteric in nature.<br />B. Beryllium carbonate is kept in the atmosphere of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;because it is thermally less stable.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BeCO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8652;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BeO</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>C. Beryllium sulphate is readily soluble in water due to high degree of hydration.</p><p>D. Beryllium shows anomalous behaviour due to small size, high ionization energy and high value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#981;</mi></math> (polarising power).</p><p>So, the correct statement is B, C and D only.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
